utils/faults/kill-nodes.py, the fault injector's harness (docs/INPROGRESS.md,
Failure, step 3), with nodes that are sleeps: a seeded schedule kills two of
three nodes and is written, a replay kills the same nodes at the same
times, and a node that it did not kill and that fails fails the run.

RUN: %kill-nodes --seed 4 --mtbf 0.2 --count 2 --log %t.schedule -- "sleep 2" "sleep 2" "sleep 2" | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ENDED
ENDED-DAG: node {{[0-2]}}: killed
ENDED-DAG: node {{[0-2]}}: killed
ENDED-DAG: node {{[0-2]}}: exited with 0
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SCHEDULE < %t.schedule
SCHEDULE: # seed=4
SCHEDULE-NEXT: {{[0-9]+}} kill {{[0-2]}}
SCHEDULE-NEXT: {{[0-9]+}} kill {{[0-2]}}
SCHEDULE-NOT: {{.}}

RUN: %kill-nodes --replay %t.schedule --log %t.replayed -- "sleep 2" "sleep 2" "sleep 2" > /dev/null
RUN: tail -n +2 %t.schedule > %t.expected
RUN: %python -c "import sys; a = [l.split() for l in open(sys.argv[1])]; b = [l.split() for l in open(sys.argv[2])]; sys.exit(not (len(a) == len(b) and all(x[2] == y[2] and abs(int(x[0]) - int(y[0])) <= 50 for x, y in zip(a, b))))" %t.expected %t.replayed

RUN: not %kill-nodes --seed 1 --mtbf 60 -- "true" "false" | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAILED
FAILED: node 0: exited with 0
FAILED-NEXT: node 1: exited with 1

--spare keeps a node from being killed: with node 0 spared, the two kills
take nodes 1 and 2. --port-from starts node 0 first and gives the port it
prints to the others as {port}; its output still comes through.
RUN: %kill-nodes --spare 0 --seed 4 --mtbf 0.1 --count 2 -- "sleep 1" "sleep 2" "sleep 2" | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SPARE
SPARE: node 0: exited with 0
SPARE-NEXT: node 1: killed
SPARE-NEXT: node 2: killed
RUN: %kill-nodes --port-from 0 --seed 1 --mtbf 60 --count 0 -- "sh -c 'echo listening 4321; sleep 0.5; echo after'" "sh -c 'echo got {port} >&2'" 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PORT
PORT-DAG: listening 4321
PORT-DAG: got 4321
PORT-DAG: after
PORT: node 0: exited with 0
PORT-NEXT: node 1: exited with 0
RUN: not %kill-nodes --port-from 0 --seed 1 --mtbf 60 --count 0 -- "true" 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOPORT
NOPORT: kill-nodes.py: node 0 ended without printing "listening PORT"
